  run_command {
    cwd: "."
    exit_code: 0
    blocking: true
    wait_ms_before_async: 5000
    combined_output {
      full: "# Call of War VTTA Virtual Tabletop (VTT) tactical system for simulating turn-based military combat between two factions (USA vs Terrorists).## Architecture- **Frontend**: React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS 4 + Vite- **Backend**: Express.js (served via Vite middleware in dev mode)- **Storage**: Firebase (optional, for images); PostgreSQL (`map_covers` table) for persistent map editor cover data- **Package Manager**: npm## Project Structure- `server.ts` \342\200\224 Express backend serving API and Vite frontend- `src/` \342\200\224 React frontend source  - `components/` \342\200\224 UI components (AdminPanel, CreateMatchMenu, MapEditorMenu, etc.)  - `contexts/` \342\200\224 React contexts (ImageContext)  - `data/constants.ts` \342\200\224 Game constants, weapon/armor/class stats  - `hooks/` \342\200\224 Custom React hooks (Firebase, Storage)  - `lib/` \342\200\224 Firebase config, utilities  - `services/` \342\200\224 API communication and storage services  - `types/game.ts` \342\200\224 TypeScript types for game entities  - `utils/` \342\200\224 Game mechanics, line of sight, image migration- `public/` \342\200\224 Static assets (map images, role icons)- `index.html` \342\200\224 App entry point## Key Features- Grid-based tactical combat (50px cells = 1.5m)- Army drafting system (100 point limit)- Cover system (None, Half, Full) \342\200\224 server-authoritative calculation- Map editor for defining cover zones- Real-time game state via polling (`/api/state` every 1.5s)- Firebase Storage integration for custom images## Turn System (server-authoritative)Each unit has 3 actions per turn that reset on `endTurn`:- **Movimento (M)** \342\200\224 one move per turn (metres governed by class + armor penalty)- **Interven\303\247\303\243o (I)** \342\200\224 needed for first shot, reload, charge (Investida) or guard activation- **T\303\241tica (T)** \342\200\224 needed for prone toggle, repositioning facing after move-lock, etc.Per-turn fields tracked on each `Unit`:`actions {move, intervention, tactical, chargeUsed}`, `shotsThisTurn`, `ammoInMag`,`movedThisTurn`, `extraMoveMeters`, `stance` (`standing`/`guard`/`prone`), `guardWatchAngle`,`facingLockedThisTurn`.## Cover System Rules### Solidez para movimento e posicionamentoC\303\251lulas marcadas como `half` (Meia Cobertura) ou `full` (Cobertura Total) s\303\243o **s\303\263lidas** \342\200\224 bloqueiam o pathfinding exatamente como `wall`. Nenhum token pode:- Passar por uma c\303\251lula `half`/`full` durante o movimento.- Pousar em uma c\303\251lula `half`/`full` como destino final (batalha ou Deploy).`water` (\303\201gua) continua atravess\303\241vel e ocup\303\241vel, com custo de movimento extra.### C\303\241lculo de cobertura (servidor autoritativo)O servidor **recalcula** a cobertura em cada tiro via `computeShotCover` \342\200\224 o cliente n\303\243o envia nem influencia `coverLevel`. O algoritmo:1. Tra\303\247a a linha de tiro (Bresenham) de atacante a alvo, ignorando as c\303\251lulas das pr\303\263prias unidades.2. Se qualquer c\303\251lula da linha for `wall` \342\206\222 tiro bloqueado.3. C\303\251lulas `full` na linha \342\206\222 `cover = \"full\"` (qualquer dist\303\242ncia).4. C\303\251lulas `half` na linha, regra de **proximidade Chebyshev \342\211\244 2**:   - Dist\303\242ncia Chebyshev(c\303\251lula, **alvo**) \342\211\244 2 \342\206\222 eleg\303\255vel a dar cobertura.   - Dist\303\242ncia Chebyshev(c\303\251lula, **atacante**) \342\211\244 2 \342\206\222 b\303\264nus cancelado (flanqueado).   - Se sobrar alguma `half` v\303\241lida e `full` ausente \342\206\222 `cover = \"half\"`.5. Em sobreposi\303\247\303\243o, `full` sempre vence.Penalidade de acerto: `half` \342\210\22220%, `full` \342\210\22240%.### Visual na batalha vs. Deploy- **Deploy**: overlays coloridos de cobertura vis\303\255veis (auxiliam posicionamento).- **Batalha**: overlays ocultos \342\200\224 o mapa fica limpo. Ao passar o mouse sobre uma c\303\251lula marcada, aparece um **tooltip flutuante** com o nome da \303\241rea (`\"Meia Cobertura\"`, `\"Cobertura Total\"`, `\"Parede\"`, `\"\303\201gua\"`, `\"Zona Deploy A/B\"`).### Combat- Hit roll d100 vs `class.hit \342\210\222 distance penalty \342\210\222 cover \342\210\222 stance modifiers`.- **Crit two-step**: on hit, second d100 vs `weapon.criticalChance` plus modifiers  (Sniper +10, Objetiva +10, Bi-p\303\251+prone +5; cover/prone reduce). Crit replaces  damage with `weapon.critical`.- Shots per turn capped by `weapon.shots`; each shot consumes one `ammoInMag`.- **Recarregar** (Intervention) refills `ammoInMag` to `weapon.reload` (magazine).### Reactive (Postura de Guarda)- Activating Guard costs Intervention and stores a watch angle.- When an enemy moves into the guard\'s FOV/arc, the server creates a  `PendingGuardShot`. The guarding player gets a modal prompting them to  confirm or skip the reactive shot. The shot pays only ammo (-10% hit  while in guard); guard ends after firing.### Other actions- **Investida** (Intervention) gives an extra movement equal to base movement.- **Jogar-se ao ch\303\243o / Levantar** (Tactical) toggles prone; prone caps move at 3m  but grants +10% defense.- **Definir \303\202ngulo** changes facing. Free before move; costs Tactical after move.### Weapon restrictionsWeapons enforce `weaponFaction` (USA/TR/Todos) and `allowedClasses` (e.g.Fuzis only for Assalto, Rifles only for Sniper). Pistols/Revolvers areavailable to all classes.## DevelopmentRun with:```npm run dev```Server starts on port 5000 (configured via `PORT` env var or defaults to 5000).## Environment Variables- `VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY` \342\200\224 Firebase API key- `VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN` \342\200\224 Firebase auth domain- `VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID` \342\200\224 Firebase project ID- `VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET` \342\200\224 Firebase storage bucket- `VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID` \342\200\224 Firebase messaging sender ID- `VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID` \342\200\224 Firebase app ID## API Endpoints- `GET /api/state` \342\200\224 Get current game state- `POST /api/move` \342\200\224 Move a unit- `POST /api/shoot` \342\200\224 Execute a shooting action- `POST /api/init` \342\200\224 Initialize a new battle- `GET /api/maps/:mapId/cover` \342\200\224 Get cover data for a map- `POST /api/maps/:mapId/cover` \342\200\224 Save cover data for a map"
    }
    command_line: "cat /tmp/call-of-war/replit.md"
    proposed_command_line: "cat /tmp/call-of-war/replit.md"
    shell_name: "bash"
  }
}
